From 7b8d21fe4f9dfa1a41cc9a07573e0ce6a44024ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 08:29:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Guarantee an unpaid app order can never reach the kitchen
 (cancel on failure)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The hold-hide should keep an abandoned/declined checkout off the KDS, but a
duplicate unpaid order reached the kitchen twice, so this adds a hard guarantee
rather than relying on the hold alone:

- The app now cancels the just-created order the instant payment fails, is
  declined, or the customer leaves the checkout without paying (unmount) — a
  CANCELED order is filtered out of the KDS everywhere, so it cannot be cooked.
  New endpoint POST /api/orders/:id/cancel, guarded to only cancel an order still
  marked bc_hold='1' with no payment (never a paid or counter order). A retry
  simply creates a fresh order. Decline copy now says 'nothing was charged'.
- The abandoned-order sweep is faster (every 2 min, cancels holds older than 5
  min instead of 30) and now only counts a cancel that actually took — the old
  code logged 'cancelled 1' even when Square refused the cancel, hiding a stuck
  order; it now logs which orders it could not cancel.
- Leak detector: the KDS logs any held order that becomes visible, with the
  reason (db-paid-marker / has-tender / order-COMPLETED / UNKNOWN), so the exact
  cause of any future leak is captured instead of guessed.

